## Architecture

```text
{{SolutionName}}/
├── src/
│   ├── {{ApiProject}}/
│   ├── {{ApplicationProject}}/
│   ├── {{DomainProject}}/
│   └── {{InfrastructureProject}}/
{{#if Docker}}├── docker-compose.yml
├── Dockerfile
├── .env.example
{{/if}}└── {{SolutionName}}.sln
```

Dependencies (all point inward):

```text
{{ApiProject}} ──► {{ApplicationProject}}, {{InfrastructureProject}}
{{InfrastructureProject}} ──► {{ApplicationProject}}, {{DomainProject}}
{{ApplicationProject}} ──► {{DomainProject}}
{{DomainProject}} ──► (no project dependencies)
```

## Prerequisites

- .NET SDK {{TargetFramework}}
- {{Database}} (local install or Docker)
- `dotnet-ef` tool: `dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef --version {{EfCoreVersion}}`
{{#if Docker}}- Docker Desktop / Docker Engine with Compose v2{{/if}}

## Run with Docker Compose

{{#if Docker}}```bash
docker compose up --build
```

`.env` was generated with a random database password and is git-ignored. The
{{#if Console}}console app runs as the `app` service. {{Database}} is at
`localhost:{{DatabasePort}}`.
{{/if}}{{#if !Console}}API is available at `http://localhost:8080`, {{Database}} at
`localhost:{{DatabasePort}}`.
{{/if}}

{{#if SqlServer}}The SQL Server container starts empty; the `{{DatabaseName}}`
database is created by the first migration.
{{/if}}To apply migrations automatically when the container starts, set
`APPLY_MIGRATIONS=true` in `.env`.
{{/if}}{{#if !Docker}}Docker files were not generated for this solution.
{{/if}}

## Run locally

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
```

Set the connection string through an environment variable (recommended) or
`appsettings.Development.json`:

```bash
{{#if Postgres}}export ConnectionStrings__Default="Host=localhost;Port={{DatabasePort}};Database={{DatabaseName}};Username={{DatabaseUser}};Password=..."
{{/if}}{{#if SqlServer}}export ConnectionStrings__Default="Server=localhost,{{DatabasePort}};Database={{DatabaseName}};User Id={{DatabaseUser}};TrustServerCertificate=True
Database__Password=..."
{{/if}}dotnet run --project src/{{ApiProject}}
```

## EF Core migrations

```bash
dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate \
  --project src/{{InfrastructureProject}} \
  --startup-project src/{{ApiProject}} \
  --output-dir Persistence/Migrations

dotnet ef database update \
  --project src/{{InfrastructureProject}} \
  --startup-project src/{{ApiProject}}
```

Migrations are not applied automatically.

{{#if Console}}## What the console app does

`dotnet run --project src/{{ApiProject}}` creates a sample product and prints
the product list. The database named in the connection string must be reachable.
{{/if}}{{#if !Console}}## API endpoints

| Method | Route | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GET | `/health` | Health probe |
| GET | `/api/products` | List products |
| GET | `/api/products/{id}` | Get a product |
| POST | `/api/products` | Create a product |

OpenAPI document (Development only): `/openapi/v1.json`.
Swagger UI (Development only): `/swagger`.
